Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:29:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(generator): induce fault and alarm scenarios (F-93,
 F-94)

--scenarios <file|demo> induces single-, two- and three-phase openings,
faults on two branches of one node, openings separated by configurable gaps
around the grouping window (--grouping-window, default 5 min), loss of
voltage, transformer phase drop, overload, low device energy, inactivity,
free fall and solar-panel alarm. Each scenario changes the telemetry of its
devices, adds an uplink at the state change and, when the Technical Annex
defines an event code, writes the SET/CLEAR/MSG rows in alarms. The CLI
prints what the platform should show for each one. Without --scenarios the
data is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
